    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look toward a favorable slate today, spearheaded by **Gunnar Henderson** (63.69) and **Heliot Ramos** (63.06). **Gunnar Henderson** remains a priority start despite the platoon disadvantage against Weathers; his positioning in the #2 hole and the matchup against a high-SB-conceding starter gives him an elite edge in our scarcest category. **Heliot Ramos** benefits from the highest upside matchup on the board, facing Sasaki\u2019s 5.30 xERA; his position as the primary offensive engine today is bolstered by significant SP skill suppression, making him our most reliable anchor. While **Coby Mayo** (60.25) draws the same starter, his dynamic platoon splits and the \"Slow SP Delivery\" bonus\u2014which we heavily weight for stolen base potential\u2014justify his inclusion in the starting nine over lower-ceiling alternatives.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Josh Jung** (48.40), who narrowly missed the cut. While he offers stability, the optimizer favored **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (58.38) and **Nolan Schanuel** (51.34) due to their superior xwOBA metrics and projected plate appearance volume. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Andy Pages** (43.51), whose score is suppressed by McDonald\u2019s 2.60 xERA; he remains a marginal start strictly to avoid wasting a game cap on a superior asset during a tougher matchup. We continue to monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.**, who remains sidelined on the IL, while keeping **Jackson Merrill**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Drake Baldwin**, **Jorge Polanco**, **Josh Lowe**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Brady House**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Dominic Smith**, and **Liam Hicks** on high alert should lineup volatility shift our efficiency projections as first pitch approaches. **Kyle Tucker** (53.52) also warrants observation; despite a difficult pairing with McDonald, his spot in the #4 order slot provides just enough leverage to maintain his utility.",
